cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HyperShield benchmark: simulation code and results for space-ground tracking of maneuvering hypersonic glide targets"
version: "1"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/labibibnmuzahid/hypershield-benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: "Al Junayed"
    given-names: "Abdullah"
    email: junayed.mahin@iubat.education
    affiliation: "International University of Business Agriculture and Technology (IUBAT)"
  - family-names: "Ibn Muzahid"
    given-names: "Labib"
    email: labib@iubat.education
    affiliation: "International University of Business Agriculture and Technology (IUBAT)"
keywords:
  - hypersonic glide vehicle
  - multi-sensor fusion
  - space-based infrared
  - target tracking
  - interacting multiple model
  - filter consistency
abstract: >-
  Scenario and sensor generators, four tracking estimators (EKF-CV, UKF-CV, EKF-CA,
  IMM-CV/CA), track management, metrics, 31 verification tests, analysis and plotting
  scripts, and the result files behind every table and figure of the paper
  "Uncertainty-aware space-ground sensor fusion for tracking maneuvering hypersonic
  targets: A reproducible simulation benchmark".
